 ## Background
-The method is based on the Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) algorithm for ray tracing, originally described by Amanatides and Woo in 1987 [S3, unofficial]. It is a fundamental technique in voxel-based rendering, often used in games and real-time applications for collision detection and volume visualization [S1, S5, unofficial]. The approach distinguishes itself from general volume raycasting by treating voxels as discrete integer-valued entities rather than continuous functions, requiring explicit floor operations for coordinate mapping [S3, unofficial].
